From 69eedb6e2ec073ca1f76ac444d55e7929920c920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:19:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Text sources: gen_text.py takes a text bank by key and
 encodes the mod font's glyphs; the lab menu, the keeper's box labels and the
 calendar title keyed

tools/gen_text.py reads text-bank.json ($TEXT_BANK), written by the project's tools/build-full.sh for TEXT=<source>:
{"font": {char: code}, "text": {key: text}}. A key replaces the yaml's text of that entry (<dir>.<SYMBOL>,
<dir>.<BLOCK>, <dir>.<BLOCK>.<index>); a character of the mod executable's extra glyphs (F040.., docs/mods/font.md)
encodes as its two-byte code instead of failing as not Shift-JIS. An empty bank gives the same headers as before.
A strings block with storage: define writes #define SYMBOL "text": literals of the code become keys without changing
the binary. Keyed so: the lab menu (text/main/mod_lab.yaml, main.LAB_STR_*), the item keeper's "In hand" and
"Keeping" (shop.STR_IN_HAND, shop.STR_KEEPING) and the arena calendar's "Tournament" (dget.DGET_STR_TOURNAMENT).
The headers depend on text-bank.json (mk/text.mk).
